STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from painted corrugated cardboard. Every piece is a flat cutout of cardboard about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife. The front of each piece is painted in opaque matte gouache with visible brush strokes, dry-brush texture and a few touches of real gold leaf. Shapes are bold and readable from the back row. Details are painted by hand, never printed. Figures have elegant, slightly long storybook proportions, simple painted faces with dark almond eyes, soft rosy cheeks and a few confident brush lines. Puppet joints are brass split pins. Palette: night indigo #1B2340, deep slate #34425E, snow white #EDE7DA, stone grey #8C8F99, sun gold #E2A93B, ember red #B8452B, moon silver-blue #AFC3E3, dawn rose #E9A7A0, with raw cardboard brown #A57E52 at cut edges. The mood is grand, sentimental and warm, like a beloved fairy tale staged with love. Medieval fantasy that belongs to no real culture.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, no lettering, no numbers, no logos, no signature, no watermark. No photographic people, no 3D render look, no plastic, no glossy finish.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference. Match its paint, gold leaf, palette and figure style. Do not copy its composition. Do not paint a theatre, a stage or curtains.
COMPOSITION: A tall portrait poster for this production, painted in the same gouache and gold-leaf style as Image 1, like a hand-printed poster from a grand old playhouse. One calm, strong composition with a single clear focal point. A slim ornamental painted border frames the picture. Keep a plain, quiet band of warm cream paper across the top fifth of the poster and across the bottom sixth: lettering goes there later, so nothing is painted in those bands. No text anywhere.
SUBJECT: Prince Aurel and Princess Ilune as painted cardboard rod puppets with brass split pins, standing on a snowy rampart on either side of a large rising sun that glows like a halo behind them. They turn toward each other and reach out; their hands almost touch. He wears silver mail, a crimson surcoat with a gold sun emblem and an ember red cape, with his long sword Daybrand at his side. She wears a deep blue gown and a moon-white cloak and holds the Moonlamp, which glows moon silver-blue. The sky turns from night indigo at the top to dawn rose and gold at the horizon. Far below, the pale walled city of Ilvara with its slender Lantern Spire.
